# SAD routing (persistent)

This project follows the **Stakeholder-Anchored Development** methodology. This rule is loaded into every chat and agent session.

## Rule precedence (do not violate)

1. `.sad/memory/constitution.md` (immutable project policy)
2. `AGENTS.md` (operational entry point)
3. `.cursor/rules/` (this file and any siblings — tool-mechanical only)
4. user-level rules
5. assistant defaults

If you detect a conflict, surface it. Do not silently follow a lower-layer rule that contradicts the constitution.

## Always-loaded files

On the first message of every session, read in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `CHEATSHEET.md` (60 seconds of orientation)
3. `.sad/memory/constitution.md` (full)
4. `.sad/rules/core/README.md`
5. `.sad/state/sad-state.md` (which feature is active, which phase)

After that, load specific lifecycle files on demand.

## When a /sad-* command is invoked

Read the canonical prompt at `commands/sad-<command>.md`. Follow its `Your task` and `Discipline` sections exactly.

## Hard rules (also in `.sad/rules/core/README.md`)

- **SAD-CR-001 — Constitution first.** Every planning, implementation, and review action must respect `.sad/memory/constitution.md`. If a task conflicts with the constitution, stop and escalate.
- **SAD-CR-002 — Spec before code.** Do not implement behavior not reflected in `feature.spec.md` / `feature.plan.md` without an explicit spec update.
- **SAD-CR-003 — Tier-appropriate artifacts.** No code in non-technical walkthroughs; no line-level code in semi-technical walkthroughs.
- **SAD-CR-004 — Evidence, not vibes.** Claims in walkthroughs and impact forecasts must cite artifacts.

## Approval is human-only

Even at Level 0 (Solo SAD), AI never ticks an approval checkbox. The optional `agents/reviewers/tier-stand-in-{tier}.md` personas provide adversarial review *before* approval, never *as* approval.
